    "question": {
      ":question/id": "66f5c774-ec8d-5973-832e-6325288b7bf8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-z &=20 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & -1 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 0 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-5R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5 \\\\ y &=4 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=5$, $y=4$, and $z=5$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle 5,4,5\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
